<v Anand>Like, "This guy's a genius." Like, "Look, so fast, a perfect

01:03:08.700 --> 01:03:13.340
<v Anand>result, exactly what I wanted." Because Ankur knew exactly what he wanted.

01:03:13.340 --> 01:03:16.140
<v Anand>He was able to communicate it so clearly that Claude was able

01:03:16.140 --> 01:03:19.340
<v Anand>to do it. And he needed a translator, someone who could take

01:03:19.340 --> 01:03:22.560
<v Anand>that, transcribe, give it to Claude, take that output, put it into

01:03:22.560 --> 01:03:25.700
<v Anand>some kind of a deployment system that he can just visit.

01:03:26.080 --> 01:03:27.620
<v Anand>That was therefore that was required.

01:03:27.700 --> 01:03:32.020
<v Anand>Now, this is a problem that was solved exceptionally well without the

01:03:32.020 --> 01:03:34.700
<v Anand>person who's in the middle understanding it.

01:03:34.700 --> 01:03:37.560
<v Anand>So I think there is also a need to understand when understanding

01:03:37.560 --> 01:03:41.980
<v Anand>is not required. I do not understand how hardware works.

01:03:42.240 --> 01:03:44.260
<v Anand>I don't know how my phone works.

01:03:44.260 --> 01:03:45.000
<v Anand>Can I use it?

01:03:45.000 --> 01:03:45.680
<v Anand>Can I not use it?

01:03:45.680 --> 01:03:47.400
<v Anand>Who cares? It works, right?

01:03:49.030 --> 01:03:50.130
<v Student>Hmm.

01:03:50.960 --> 01:03:53.920
<v Student>But still, the customer thing I'm still a little bit—

01:03:53.920 --> 01:03:56.260
<v Anand>Well, if it doesn't work, then—

01:03:56.260 --> 01:04:00.940
<v Student>Has anyone started using—like, has anyone, have they started progressing towards these

01:04:00.940 --> 01:04:01.440
<v Student>things?

01:04:01.160 --> 01:04:05.120
<v Anand>Let me put it this way: have you ever seen any chat

01:04:05.120 --> 01:04:07.700
<v Anand>interface in any customer service that is answered by an AI?

01:04:08.240 --> 01:04:09.340
<v Student>Yeah, yeah, I did.

01:04:09.340 --> 01:04:10.340
<v Kusuma>They are yet to.

01:04:10.340 --> 01:04:12.280
<v Student>Still they are still transitioning.

01:04:12.280 --> 01:04:13.480
<v Student>It's not that good.

01:04:13.880 --> 01:04:17.740
<v Anand>When I opened Airtel, for instance, this morning, it was answered by

01:04:17.740 --> 01:04:18.840
<v Anand>AI.

01:04:21.540 --> 01:04:26.260
<v Anand>Practically, every service that I'm seeing has some kind of an AI

01:04:26.260 --> 01:04:28.400
<v Anand>chatbot behind the scenes.

01:04:28.440 --> 01:04:31.120
<v Student>But most of the time it's like an if-else only, like if

01:04:31.120 --> 01:04:32.840
<v Student>this question is asked, you answer this.

01:04:32.980 --> 01:04:36.800
<v Anand>Possibly. And if that is the case, then the chatbot will over

01:04:36.800 --> 01:04:39.560
<v Anand>time improve. But here's the thing, right, whether it's if-else rules or

01:04:39.560 --> 01:04:40.980
<v Anand>AI, it is not a human.

01:04:41.080 --> 01:04:42.460
<v Student>Yeah, it's not a human, at least.

01:04:42.460 --> 01:04:44.210
<v Anand>AI is better than an if-else, in any case.

01:04:44.210 --> 01:04:47.400
<v Anand>If you're saying, "I'm happy to put something as rubbish as an

01:04:47.700 --> 01:04:48.300
<v Anand>if-else"—

01:04:48.300 --> 01:04:51.680
<v Student>It will have to progressively, over time, improve.

01:04:52.050 --> 01:04:52.720
<v Student>Yes.

01:04:52.720 --> 01:04:54.660
<v Anand>Which makes sense. Definitely.

01:04:54.660 --> 01:04:57.260
<v Anand>What I'm saying is not that it is right or wrong, but

01:04:57.260 --> 01:05:00.520
<v Anand>rather that people are already comfortable doing it.

01:05:00.520 --> 01:05:04.320
<v Anand>The fact that you are uncomfortable means perhaps that you haven't yet

01:05:04.320 --> 01:05:07.560
<v Anand>noticed the sheer number of people who are already doing it.

01:05:07.770 --> 01:05:12.500
<v Student>No, yes. Because even I tried building a chatbot, a RAG chatbot

01:05:12.640 --> 01:05:16.440
<v Student>because of There was this In my office, I work as—

01:05:16.440 --> 01:05:18.325
<v Anand>You aren't mic'd up.

01:05:18.500 --> 01:05:20.575
<v Kusuma>the voice will be Voice will be fine.

01:05:20.575 --> 01:05:21.372
<v Anand>Will carry? Okay, sorry.

01:05:21.372 --> 01:05:21.872
<v Anand>Huh.

01:05:21.524 --> 01:05:22.980
<v Student>But I'm bothered the mic can pick it.

01:05:23.000 --> 01:05:25.940
<v Student>I was saying that, yeah, I tried building a chatbot of course,

01:05:25.940 --> 01:05:27.040
<v Student>I didn't know about RAG.

01:05:27.040 --> 01:05:32.360
<v Student>I was still learning about RAG, as embeddings, chunking, vector database, everything.

01:05:32.360 --> 01:05:33.260
<v Student>I didn't know much of it.

01:05:33.260 --> 01:05:35.068
<v Student>I just started with my Codex.

01:05:35.068 --> 01:05:35.960
<v Student>Well, not with Codex, with ChatGPT only.

01:05:35.960 --> 01:05:38.020
<v Student>I told him that this is my problem.

01:05:38.020 --> 01:05:40.020
<v Student>I want to make a chatbot for it, right.

01:05:40.020 --> 01:05:42.660
<v Student>Because support questions, like we had got a lot of support questions

01:05:42.660 --> 01:05:46.000
<v Student>in our office and there is one lady who keeps answering these

01:05:46.000 --> 01:05:48.060
<v Student>questions like Because most of the questions are repetitive.

01:05:48.200 --> 01:05:50.220
<v Student>They're asking what is the fee, what is the course, what's the

01:05:50.220 --> 01:05:51.670
<v Student>professor, what are the timings.

01:05:51.800 --> 01:05:53.300
<v Student>I was like, we will just build a chatbot.

01:05:53.300 --> 01:05:56.680
<v Student>Yeah, they never implemented on the main site, but yeah, I was

01:05:56.680 --> 01:05:59.350
<v Student>happy. I mean, yeah, I was able to solve a lot of

01:05:59.350 --> 01:06:04.080
<v Student>her problems, a lot of things which can be automated because many

01:06:04.080 --> 01:06:06.413
<v Student>of the questions are, you know, repetitive questions.

01:06:06.413 --> 01:06:08.395
<v Student>So why keep answering them again and again?

01:06:08.395 --> 01:06:11.800
<v Anand>And I've seen this pattern a lot, which is that personal software

01:06:11.800 --> 01:06:14.740
<v Anand>seems to be an easier entry point than enterprise software.

01:06:14.740 --> 01:06:18.420
<v Anand>If I say I have to deploy this in the IITM chatbot

01:06:18.420 --> 01:06:20.460
<v Anand>website, then there'll be 20 rules.

01:06:20.920 --> 01:06:23.800
<v Anand>If all I have to do is for the requests that come

01:06:23.800 --> 01:06:26.640
<v Anand>to me, I have to use an AI to solve the problem,

01:06:26.640 --> 01:06:30.420
<v Anand>I can just, worst case, copy-paste, get the answer, send it or

01:06:30.420 --> 01:06:34.600
<v Anand>create a little tool that automatically does that, or even creates a

01:06:34.600 --> 01:06:37.260
<v Anand>draft so that I can just look at, review, approve, et cetera.

01:06:37.260 --> 01:06:41.280
<v Anand>I have to ask fewer people, and the impact is also less.

01:06:41.300 --> 01:06:44.560
<v Anand>And it's so easy for people to build tools for themselves, or

01:06:44.560 --> 01:06:48.220
<v Anand>get someone like you to build the tool for them, that individual

01:06:48.220 --> 01:06:53.240
<v Anand>productivity is growing faster than organizational productivity.

01:06:53.520 --> 01:06:54.820
<v Anand>Which is not a bad thing.

01:06:54.900 --> 01:06:57.400
<v Anand>What that means is at least the people who are catching on

01:06:57.400 --> 01:07:03.480
<v Anand>to this are able to progress further in their career relative to

01:07:03.480 --> 01:07:06.160
<v Anand>others who are not yet catching on to this.

01:07:06.440 --> 01:07:09.520
<v Anand>Which is what is leading people to say, "It's not AI that

01:07:09.520 --> 01:07:10.440
<v Anand>you need to be worried about.

01:07:10.440 --> 01:07:12.540
<v Anand>It is a person using AI that you need to be worried

01:07:12.540 --> 01:07:15.490
<v Anand>about." But I don't see that as being a bad thing, because

01:07:15.490 --> 01:07:17.440
<v Anand>a person who is not using AI then starts looking at the

01:07:17.440 --> 01:07:22.500
<v Anand>person who's using AI, "Okay, fine, let me now start and overall,

01:07:22.700 --> 01:07:26.640
<v Anand>there's productivity gain." A productivity gain does not necessarily translate to more

01:07:26.640 --> 01:07:30.410
<v Anand>happiness, because we always want to earn more than our neighbors, so

01:07:30.410 --> 01:07:33.140
<v Anand>there's competition and that'll even things out and all that, yeah.

01:07:33.160 --> 01:07:34.980
<v Anand>But at least it leads to more productivity.
